Aldo Pignotti <apig@yermudder.com> writes:

> Dr. Strangelove wrote:
> > 
> > >Derek Elder wrote:
> > > Is there an easy way in software with DEC UNIX 4.0 to stripe
> > > (raid 0) a couple disks into one large virtual partition?
> > 
> > You'll need a separate RAID controller I'm afraid, which aren't
> > exactly cheap.
> > 
> no, all you need is lsm.  it is just a repackaged (and old)
> version of veritas. you can do raid 0 very easily.

LSM _will_ cost you though, if you haven't gotten the licenses along
with a server or something. LSM will also add another layer in the OS
between filesystem and physical disk thus adding overhead.

Being aware that the issue really is RAID 0 in _software_ i still have
to recommend an inexpensive hardware RAID controller - if simplicity
and performance is allowed to cost a little.

For example, the CMD CRD-5400 (see www.cmd.com) with one host and to
disk SCSI controllers is a good and not too expensive choice.

