I'd put an E10000 up against an Origin 2000 any day of the week. With the CrayLink, SGI solved
one of the problems of the "LAN in a can" NUMA clusters - bandwidth between CPU systems -
but they can't do much about the latency, which means that the scalability drops off significantly
faster than linear as you add CPUs. The E1000 scales at 92% of linear from 4 to 64 CPUs, and
does even better than that up to 48.

