> to the E10000?  Care to compare the hoards of droids it takes to
> keep a Sysplex operating?

I suspect he's talking IBM MIPS. In those, the E10000 comes in at about twice the Hitachi
Skyline, which is itself a good bit faster than anything IBM is putting out now. The E10000
also has significantly more I/O bandwidth and aggregate throughput than the Hitachi.

> I guess there are still lots of people with blue pinstripe glazing
> on their glasses :-)

Yup. IBM stock is back up over $100. :-)


