whughes@excalib.com wrote:
> 
> What (IF any) are the differences in the Digital UNIX 4.0 kernel for a
> normal system vs. one that is clustered?  I have some s/w that all my
> other customers use fine on 4.0 but one who uses a clustered system and
> claims the software doesn't work due to the fact that the kernel is
> different. If this is the case where would I get more info, there wasn't
> much I could find at www.digital.com

Do they use the TruCluster Production Server or just the Available
Server (ie do they have a Memory Channel interface) ?

Both AS and PS installs a SCSI driver (the AM driver) to be able to do
pings across the Shared SCSI bus.

If they do have MC, then the kernel contains the drivers for the MC as
well.

The Shared SCSI bus is normally also bumped up to 16 (because all
machines in the cluster should have the same SCSI bus number for the
shared SCSI).

Having said all this, I am very doubtful that this is the problem, it
would be helpful if you could explain what the software does (or does
do) when running in the cluster.

