On Fri, 05 Dec 1997 08:20:23 GMT, khw@earthlink.net wrote:
[snip]
>I have setup latcp correctly (by running latsetup)

latsetup only creates LAT devices and a few bits of other setup. You
need a latstartup.conf file in /etc which should consist of lines
using the latcp command to map the DEC server hardware ethernet
address and port numbers to physical tty devices. I can't  remember
the syntax of latcp off the top of my head, but it's something like:

latcp -A -ptty?? -HLAT_{h/w ethernet address} -R{rort name}

check out the man page for the correct syntax.

>
>I also tried couple commands to make both terminal servers and DEC
>UNIX to talk, so I can make it as a printer server. I have tried many
>of the commands that are described in the Digital UNIX Network
>administration guid, but I have not been able to print or make both
>terminal server and DEC UNIX to communicate. I have some ideas on how
>to setup the printcap file, but before doing that, I have to make both
>DEC UNIX and terminal server talk!!!!

The printcap file should reffer to the device you've previously mapped
with the latcp command using a device type of either dev or lat (there
doesn't seem to be a huge amount of difference between them).

Hope this helps.


