Looks like someone's been dumpster diving.  I don't have any of the old
monitor data at hand so the following is based on very old web pages
and notes sitting around.  You also don't mention which card version you
have.  The following is for the ZLX-E (PMAGD-AA -BA and -CA) and ZLXp-E
series and should be in some of the documents:


Resolution settings



Switch  Pixel Rate   Res.    Refresh     Monitors
Setting   (MHz)               (Hz)



   0      130     1280x1024    72      A B C D E F G
   1      119     1280x1024    66      B C D E G H I J K
   2      108     1280x1024    60
   3      104     1152x900     72
   4       93     1152x900     66      G
   5       75     1024x768     70      D
   6       74     1024x768     72      A D G J
   7       69     1024x864     60      G L M
   8       65     1024x768     60      D J
   9       50      800x600     72      G
   A       40      800x600     60      G
   B       32      640x480     72      D G J
   C       25      640x480     60      G




Monitor Code           Designation



     A                 VRM17-HA/H4/AA/A4
     B                 VRT19-HA/H4
     C                 VRT16-HA/H4
     D                 VRC16-HA/H4
     E                 VR320-DA
     F                 VR319-DA
     G                 VRC21-HA
     H                 VRT19-DA/D3/D4
     I                 VRT16-DA/D3/D4
     J                 VRC16-CA/C4
     K                 VR319-CA
     L                 VR297
     M                 VR299



ZLX-L's and -M's are going to be 1280x1024.  Newer 4D40T and better cards
support many modes but no 1152x870 (1152x900 yes).

Also, the VRT-19HA is a 1280x1024 dual frequency monitor (66 or 72 Hz)
according to some text in front of me.  However, this source has a few
errors such as the old VRE01 electroluminescent display being 1280x1024
when it's really 1024x864.  Or perhaps you have an Oz special...

And what's 'DecUnix 3.5'?

m


